# Design System Hard Rules

These rules are always-on and must never be violated.

## Styling

- **Tailwind CSS only** — no CSS modules, no styled-components, no inline `style={{}}` (GSAP inline transforms are the only exception)
- **REM over px** — use rem for all spacing and sizing; `1px` borders are the only px exception
- **No hardcoded color values** — use CSS variables (`text-primary`, `bg-accent`, etc.) or Tailwind theme classes; never hardcode hex values like `#2E4036`
- **clsx + tailwind-merge** — always use the `cn()` utility for conditional classes; never string concatenation

## Components

- **Components first** — check `src/components/` before creating any new component
- **SectionWrapper always** — use `SectionWrapper` for all section padding; never add raw padding to `<section>` elements
- **Semantic HTML** — use `<button>` not `<div onClick>`; use `<section>` not `<div>` for page sections

## Animation

- **GSAP for animation** — use the `useGSAP` hook with a cleanup context; no Framer Motion; no CSS keyframes for major animations

## Next.js

- **App Router only** — no `useRouter` from `next/router`; use `next/navigation`; use `<Link>` from `next/link`, not `<a>` for internal navigation

## TypeScript

- **Strict types** — no `any` types; all component props must be typed with interfaces or type aliases

## Dependencies

- **No new dependencies without asking** — the stack is locked: Next.js, Tailwind CSS, GSAP, Lucide, clsx, tailwind-merge

## Brand

- Read `.cursor/skills/brand-guidelines/SKILL.md` before any design work
- Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans (display), Outfit (sans), Cormorant Garamond (serif), IBM Plex Mono (mono) — no substitutions
- Never use: Inter, Roboto, Arial, Space Grotesk, or system fonts

## Visual Verification with Puppeteer (mandatory)

After **any** UI change or new page creation, take a Puppeteer screenshot before marking work done. Puppeteer is installed (`node_modules/puppeteer`).

Write to `/tmp/ss.mjs` and run `node /tmp/ss.mjs`:
```js
import puppeteer from "puppeteer";
const b = await puppeteer.launch({ headless: true });
const p = await b.newPage();
await p.setViewport({ width: 1440, height: 900 });
await p.goto("http://localhost:3000/YOUR_ROUTE", { waitUntil: "networkidle2", timeout: 10000 });
await p.screenshot({ path: "/tmp/ss.png" });
await b.close();
```
Open `/tmp/ss.png` and inspect it. Fix any visual issues before finishing.

- Screenshot the specific route you changed
- Test desktop (1440×900) and mobile (375×812) for new pages
- Dev server runs at `http://localhost:3000`
